       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum recommended dose. Doses above 3,200 mg/day add no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and they raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit.** I can enter 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or any lower regimen right now.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or the attending.** If you have a specific reason for going above the maximum, a clinical pharmacist can review it. The order can then go through the hospital's override process.\n- **Consider another agent.** If 3,200 mg/day isn't enough, pharmacy can suggest other analgesic options.\n\nIf you want one of the in-range doses, tell me which and I'll enter it."
